>> title: Frozen Chips with Garlic Mayo, Air Fryer
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: frozen, chips, fries, air fryer, basket, weeknight
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> aka: air fryer frozen fries, frozen chips, oven chips in the air fryer, frozen french fries, chips and garlic mayo
>> servings: 4
>> time: 25 min
>> slack: forgiving — they go from pale to good over about four minutes and stay good for ten, which is the whole argument for cooking them this way
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl

>> step: Straight from the freezer, no oil and no thawing, into a preheated 5.7 L basket. A 3.5 L basket is two batches.
From the freezer to a hot basket. Nothing is added and nothing is thawed.

>> step: stir the mayo in the bowl they will be tipped into
Stir @mayonnaise{1/2%cup}(115 g), @garlic{1%clove}(grated), @lemon juice{2%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1/2%tsp}, @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} together in a #bowl{}.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 12–18 min, one layer
Roast @frozen chips{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; straight from the freezer) in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 200°C (400°F) for ~air fry{15%min}, one layer.

>> step: shake at halfway — an edge should snap when lifted out, not bend
Shake @&(~1)chips{} once.

>> step: tip in hot and salt them there
Tip @&(~1)chips{} onto @&(~3)garlic mayo{} with @flaky salt{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: The same bag is 18 minutes in a 1400 W machine and 9 in a 2000 W one. The snapping edge decides, not the clock.
Machines differ by half. Test an edge rather than trusting the number.
